            <ArticleTitle>﻿Novel use of a local drug delivery catheter for coronary perforation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E236-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>﻿Coronary perforation is a complication of percutaneous coronary intervention that may be fatal. Conventionally, a perfusion balloon catheter is used for treatment, but may not always be available. We report a case in which bleeding due to coronary perforation was successfully treated without induction of ischemia using a local drug delivery catheter as a perfusion device.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
